le_e_atlante%2C_1513-15%2C_da_palazzo_landriani.JPG",7,4,1,0,64,null,null,null,null,48],[133514774,"madonna oggioni",1515,0,null,null,2,"b/bb/Bernardino_luini%2C_madonna_oggioni%2C_1516_circa.JPG/330px-Bernardino_luini%2C_madonna_oggioni%2C_1516_circa.JPG",7,4,1,0,64,null,null,null,null,48],[133514922,"Madonna and Child",1510,0,null,null,2,"5/5f/Bernardino_luini%2C_madonna_col_bambino%2C_1510_ca.JPG/330px-Bernardino_luini%2C_madonna_col_bambino%2C_1510_ca.JPG",2,4,1,0,65,null,null,null,null,48],[134539988,"St Catherine Carried to her Tomb by Angels",1520,0,null,null,2,"9/90/Bernardino_Luini_014.jpg/330px-Bernardino_Luini_014.jpg",0,2,1,0,0,null,null,null,"120 × 226 cm",48],[134540012,"fanciullo che coglie uva",null,0,null,null,2,"2/26/Bernardino_luini%2C_fanciullo_che_coglie_uva.JPG/330px-Bernardino_luini%2C_fanciullo_che_coglie_uva.JPG",2,4,1,0,35,null,null,null,null,48],[134540060,"ritorno di san giorgio",null,0,null,null,2,"7/77/Bernardino_luini%2C_ritorno_di_san_giorgio.JPG/330px-Bernardino_luini%2C_ritorno_di_san_giorgio.JPG",2,4,1,0,66,null,null,null,null,48],[135423003,"Madonna with Child and apple",1525,0,null,null,2,"3/34/1525_Luini_Maria_mit_dem_Kind_und_dem_Apfel_anagoria.JPG/330px-1525_Luini_Maria_mit_dem_Kind_und_dem_Apfel_anagoria.JPG",0,13,1,0,37,null,"217",null,"53 × 42 cm",48],[139058500,"The Conversion of the Magdalen",1520,0,null,null,2,"a/a3/Conversion_of_the_Magdalen_by_Luini.jpg/330px-Conversion_of_the_Magdalen_by_Luini.jpg",0,2,1,0,67,null,"1936.23","Oil on panel","64.77 × 82.55 cm",48]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaryKind":"excerpt","summaryLicenceUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","factsSource":"Wikidata (CC0)","factsFormat":2,"rankVersion":1,"summaries":{"3606183":["The Villa La Pelucca frescoes are a c. 1520–1523 cycle of frescos by Bernardino Luini, commissioned by the Milanese nobleman Gerolamo Rabia for his villa near Monza, known as 'La Pelucca'.","Villa La Pelucca frescoes"],"3661057":["Casa Atellani, or also Casa degli Atellani, is a memorial that belonged to Ludovico Sforza, Duke of Milan, the last surviving trace of the ancient Borgo delle Grazie. Historically part of the Sestiere di Porta Vercellina, today it is located at numbers 66 and 67 of Corso Magenta.","Casa Atellani"],"3697672":["Christ Among the Doctors is an oil painting on panel of c. 1510–1530 by the Italian Renaissance artist Bernardino Luini in the National Gallery, London, depicting Christ with the doctors of the law. In addition to the prime version in London, copies of varying quality also survive.","Christ Among the Doctors (Luini)"],"3842633":["Madonna of the Rose Garden is an oil painting on panel of c. 1510 by the Italian Renaissance artist Bernardino Luini. It is in the Pinacoteca di Brera in Milan, which acquired it from the Giuseppe Bianchi collection in 1826.","Madonna of the Rose Garden (Luini)"],"3945710":["Salome with the Head of John the Baptist is a c. 1527 oil-on-panel painting by Bernardino Luini. It was in the Imperial Gallery, in Vienna, until 1773, when it was swapped for another work and arrived in Florence, where it now hangs in the Uffizi Gallery.","Salome with the Head of John the Baptist (Luini)"],"17652075":["Holy Family with Saints Anne and John the Baptist is a c. 1530 oil on panel painting by Bernardino Luini.","Holy Family with Saints Anne and John the Baptist (Luini)"],"18086183":["Ecce Homo is an oil-on-panel painting executed c. 1500–1532 by the Italian Renaissance artist Bernardino Luini, now in the Wallraf-Richartz Museum in Cologne. Kurl Badt previously misattributed it to Andrea Solario, but Federico Zeri restored the correct attribution in 1971.","Ecce Homo (Luini)"],"28004411":["Ham Mocking Noah is an oil on panel painting by Italian artist Bernardino Luini, from c. 1510-1515. It is held in the Brera Gallery, in Milan.","Ham Mocking Noah"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}